  "description": "Indian oncology OPD formulary — what a med-onc / rad-onc / palliative clinic in Alwar actually writes. Cytotoxics, targeted agents, hormonals and the whole supportive-care shelf, each generic carrying the Indian brand names a doctor dictates instead of the generic. Used ONLY to decide whether a dictated drug name is known (app/formulary.py); it never rewrites a name.",
  "_comment_ayurveda": "The 89 entries tagged scope=ayurveda are MODEL-DRAFTED AND UNREVIEWED (doc 24 §4, §9). They are classical preparations and the proprietary brands an Indian OPD dictates, and they exist so the ayurveda console can be demonstrated end-to-end on LLM_PROVIDER=fake. A BAMS practitioner must review this shelf before it is enabled for real patients — the same gate the oncology tree bank sits behind. `scope` decides only which system of medicine may call a dictated name KNOWN; it is not a clinical claim about the preparation, and nothing here is a dose, an indication or an anupana.",
